Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the Fullstack Software Engineer role with CLEAR. I bring over three years of professional experience designing, building, testing, and deploying full-stack production systems with Python, React, Typescript, AWS, CI/CD pipelines, and secure API-driven architectures, along with a strong academic foundation as a Master of Science in Computer Science graduate from Pace University, NY.

Through my experience across two engineering roles, I have built and operated production systems that closely reflect CLEAR's need for engineers who can own complex technical problems from design through deployment. As a Software Engineer at Sperse, I designed and deployed a secure identity platform-adjacent multi-agent CRM system using Python, FastAPI, LangGraph, and LangChain, serving 10,000+ users through 40+ specialized sub-agents with tenant-aware access control. I also owned a React Flow and Typescript full-stack applications surface from technical discovery through rollout, partnering with Product, Design, Security, and Operations to operate reliable workflow systems in production. To keep these systems ready for customers, I built GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines for cloud-native deployments on Docker and Kubernetes, using OpenTelemetry trace-based evals to improve reliability, performance, observability, latency, accuracy, and safety before production.

Prior to Sperse, as a Software Engineer at Qualitest, I contributed to cloud infrastructure and distributed systems that users relied on daily. I designed a cloud-native Storage Service in Java, Spring Boot, PostgreSQL, and Redis with secure APIs for uploads, downloads, and deletions across S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO via expiring signed URLs. I also optimized PostgreSQL with window functions, materialized views, and indexes, then delivered React visualizations that translated business problems for stakeholders, and operated AWS infrastructure with Step Functions, Lambda, S3, and CloudWatch to improve error recovery, testing, and operational support across 100K+ weekly executions. That combination of API design, AWS operations, stakeholder communication, and production ownership is directly aligned with CLEAR's focus on reliable, scalable solutions.

I am especially drawn to CLEAR's mission to make experiences safer and easier and to enable frictionless, safe journeys using identity. The values reflected in that mission -- trust, efficiency, customer satisfaction, loyalty, and builder-minded problem solving -- match the way I approach engineering work: build simple systems, validate them in production, improve developer experience, and collaborate clearly across technical and non-technical teams. I would be excited to bring that discipline to CLEAR's identity platform and help strengthen security while creating seamless experiences across travel, enterprise, healthcare, financial services, and beyond. I would love to discuss my interest in this position with your team and can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration, I look forward to connecting!

